Test Plan for Binary Search Tree Implementation
ECE 2230, Fall 2025
Zade Hyatt

1. Details

The BST module consists of tree.h (header), tree.c (implementation), and lab5.c (test drivers).

Data structures: tree_t (root pointer, size counter, comparison counter) and node_in_tree_t (key, data pointer, left/right children).

Key features:
- Recursive insert, remove, and search operations
- Memory management: all memory freed in tree_destruct
- Comparison counting follows Standish's definitions (one comparison to check match, one additional for direction if not found)
- Removal handles three cases: no children, one child, two children (using inorder successor)

